  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 312 AM MDT SAT OCT 10 2026\nCome Tuesday, the closed upper low will sit just south of our \narea over the Great Basin as it slowly steers out east. There is\nsome uncertainty to the extent of remnant moisture carried by \nthe shifting low, but Tuesday will generally see a 15-35% chance\nof precipitation across the western Magic Valley, Boise \nMountains, and Southern Idaho Highlands as it moves off to the \neast. Thanks to the southerly flow aloft, higher snow levels \nwill limit any dusting of snow to elevations above 7000 feet, \nwith little accumulation anticipated. \n\nA warming and drying trend will set in beyond Tuesday as a following \nridge builds into the area. A shortwave trough from British Columbia \nwill dig north of our area late Wednesday through Thursday, but keep \nour area on the dry side. Thursday through Saturday, a highly \namplified Pacific ridge will build in and return a slow warming \ntrend. Temperatures 5 to 10 degrees above normal will be possible \nFriday and Saturday.",
